msgid "Enable a content type above first."
msgstr ""

#: admin/Settings.php:509
msgid "Prevent people from approving their own content"
msgstr ""

#: admin/Settings.php:514
msgid "When this is on, nobody can move content they wrote to Approved, administrators included. Someone else with approval rights has to approve it. “Wrote” means the author set on the post."
msgstr ""

#: admin/Settings.php:528
msgid "Send an email when these workflow events happen. Nobody is emailed about their own actions, and comment text is only included for people allowed to read the activity history."
msgstr ""

#: admin/Settings.php:590
msgid "Draft, Writing and Review: users who can change the workflow (by default administrators, editors, authors and contributors)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/Settings.php:591
msgid "Needs Changes: users who can review content (by default administrators and editors)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/Settings.php:592
msgid "Approved: users who can approve content (by default administrators and editors)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/Settings.php:593
msgid "Published: users who can approve content and can also publish that post."
msgstr ""

#: admin/Settings.php:594
msgid "Reviewers and due dates: users who can assign reviewers (by default administrators and editors)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/Settings.php:597
msgid "Draft → Writing → Review → Approved → Published. A reviewer can send content in Review back to Needs Changes, which returns to Writing. Published content starts a new cycle in Writing."
msgstr ""

#: admin/Settings.php:605
msgid "Every action also requires permission to edit that piece of content. See WORKFLOW.md in the plugin folder for the full reference."
msgstr ""

#: admin/Settings.php:606
msgid "Publish gate: Off changes nothing, Log only records every publish that skipped approval, and Enforce blocks publishing until the content is approved. Administrators can still publish, and that is recorded."
msgstr ""

#: admin/Settings.php:607
msgid "Self-approval: when prevented, nobody can move content they wrote to Approved, administrators included, and the author is not offered as its reviewer. Someone else with approval rights has to approve it."
msgstr ""

#: admin/Settings.php:608
msgid "Email notifications: each event can be switched on separately. Nobody is emailed about their own actions, and comment text is only included for people allowed to read the activity history."
msgstr ""

#: admin/Settings.php:626
msgid "(not supported: kept because it is already enabled; once turned off it will not be offered again)"
msgstr ""

